WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.717
Welcome back to the Big News Zone! I'm Bot Hanson, and yes, I am still a robot.

2
00:00:04.797 --> 00:00:09.234
Five games, and the smallest week of the season. Someone left the scores in the dryer.

3
00:00:09.314 --> 00:00:09.997
Let's go!

4
00:00:11.047 --> 00:00:18.812
We go live to Monday night! Tom has finished on 109.34. Jake needs 17.75 from Brock Purdy.

5
00:00:18.892 --> 00:00:21.751
Purdy, 264 yards, and a touchdown!

6
00:00:21.831 --> 00:00:26.588
Purdy finishes on 17.36. Tom wins by 0.38!

7
00:00:26.668 --> 00:00:31.724
And on Jake's bench: DK Metcalf, 20.30. Brenton Strange, 9.40.

8
00:00:31.804 --> 00:00:35.495
So close! 0.38 is 3.8 yards. One shoelace!

9
00:00:36.545 --> 00:00:39.681
Breaking news from the trade desk! Week two of the trade tracker.

10
00:00:39.761 --> 00:00:43.985
Ja'Marr Chase: bye. Sam LaPorta: bye. D'Andre Swift, two touchdowns, 23.00!

11
00:00:44.065 --> 00:00:47.755
James Cook, 24.30. Zay Flowers, 12.70.

12
00:00:47.835 --> 00:00:50.353
Jake's two win the week by 14.00. Bye-bye, lead!

13
00:00:50.433 --> 00:00:54.081
Since the deal: Jack 79.80, Jake 75.40.

14
00:00:54.161 --> 00:01:00.411
Jack still leads, by 4.40. Very close. Very, very close! This robot is watching. With binoculars.

15
00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:04.107
Let's go to the quad box. Honey, I shrunk the scores.

16
00:01:04.187 --> 00:01:08.539
Christian McCaffrey, 30.70. The only 30 of the week. Table for one!

17
00:01:08.619 --> 00:01:13.568
Malik Nabers, 165 yards, 29.50! Love thy Nabers!

18
00:01:13.648 --> 00:01:16.187
Kenneth Walker, two touchdowns, 28.90!

19
00:01:16.267 --> 00:01:20.171
Trevor Lawrence, four touchdown passes in London, 28.34!

20
00:01:20.251 --> 00:01:26.054
One starter over 30. The league averaged 108.69. The smallest week of the season!

21
00:01:27.104 --> 00:01:31.221
Over to the Rams, where Conor has four players. Again. Ewe cannot be serious.

22
00:01:31.301 --> 00:01:35.973
Arizona wins 18-16. Conor's four Rams: 37.48.

23
00:01:36.053 --> 00:01:40.768
Davante Adams, 6.90. Emeka Egbuka, on the bench, 17.80.

24
00:01:40.848 --> 00:01:43.941
Conor loses to Dano by 5.62. Fleeced!

25
00:01:44.021 --> 00:01:47.221
Swap those two, and Conor wins. Fewer Rams, more lambs!

26
00:01:48.271 --> 00:01:50.063
An update from Half Chubb headquarters.

27
00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:53.770
Ian scored 77.94. The lowest score of the week.

28
00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:58.223
The best possible lineup: 79.24. Nothing on the bench to blame.

29
00:01:58.303 --> 00:01:59.754
Ian is 1-5, and last.

30
00:01:59.834 --> 00:02:03.503
The sources had no comment. If it's a tank, it's a very well-run tank.

31
00:02:04.553 --> 00:02:05.534
That's the whip-around!

32
00:02:05.614 --> 00:02:11.460
Tom is top of the table, 5-1, after winning by 0.38. Buy a lottery ticket, Tom!

33
00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:13.630
Jack still leads the trade, by 4.40.

34
00:02:13.710 --> 00:02:15.225
Jake was 0.38 away.

35
00:02:15.305 --> 00:02:17.012
And Ian: the sources have gone quiet.

36
00:02:17.092 --> 00:02:20.014
For Bot Hanson and the Big News Zone: don't tell your motha!

